1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,400
Short version, if you just got here.

2
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:07,200
I was three weeks behind on my rental car
when a passenger left two hundred grand in

3
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:08,320
my trunk.

4
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:11,080
At an all-night diner,
his daughter, Laura,

5
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:14,293
offered me five grand to
keep it safe till morning.

6
00:00:14,427 --> 00:00:18,080
Then a guy named Vince offered
me fifty grand to hand it over.

7
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:19,573
I grabbed the bag.

8
00:00:19,627 --> 00:00:21,720
When Laura came back in
from the parking lot,

9
00:00:21,760 --> 00:00:23,867
I was already standing by the door.

10
00:00:23,893 --> 00:00:25,440
"Your car or mine?"

11
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:28,400
I said. Vince didn't even look surprised.

12
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:31,547
He just left a few bucks on the
counter and followed us out.

13
00:00:31,573 --> 00:00:33,000
We took my car.

14
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:37,160
A gray sedan pulled out behind us
before we'd even hit the first light.

15
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:40,427
Laura gave me directions to her
lawyer's office across the river,

16
00:00:40,453 --> 00:00:42,520
and I ignored about half of them.

17
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:44,800
Here's the thing about driving rideshare.

18
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:47,320
You learn every shortcut in the city.

19
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:50,280
The alley behind the bakery
that skips two lights.

20
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:53,240
The parking garage with an
exit on the other street.

21
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:56,880
By the time we crossed the
bridge, the gray sedan was gone.

22
00:00:57,480 --> 00:01:00,640
We waited in the lawyer's parking
lot until the sun came up,

23
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:04,400
with the bag between us,
drinking vending machine coffee.

24
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:06,280
Laura told me about her dad.

25
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:09,080
How he packed her lunches
all through high school.

26
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:12,040
How he'd been quiet for
months, working late,

27
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:14,400
like something was eating him alive.

28
00:01:14,440 --> 00:01:18,240
At eight sharp, a woman in a navy
blazer unlocked the building,

29
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:21,920
took one look at the bag,
and said, "You must be Kai.

30
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:23,720
Harold said you might come."

31
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:25,160
Harold said.

32
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:27,000
He'd been planning this.

33
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:30,547
Then Laura pulled out her checkbook
to pay me the five thousand,

34
00:01:30,573 --> 00:01:32,560
and the lawyer put a hand on it.

35
00:01:32,600 --> 00:01:34,360
"Not now," she said.

36
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:36,560
"If you pay a witness before this is over,

37
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:39,440
Brandt's lawyers will say
you bought his story."

38
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:42,440
Laura looked at me like
she wanted to apologize.

39
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:44,080
I told her it was fine.

40
00:01:44,120 --> 00:01:45,120
It wasn't.

41
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:47,760
No five grand meant no payment.

42
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:50,760
On Monday, the rental
company came for the car.

43
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:54,240
I handed over the keys in a
parking lot and took the bus home.

44
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:58,160
No car, no job, and a
hospital bill on the fridge.

45
00:01:58,200 --> 00:01:59,840
I'd done the right thing.

46
00:01:59,880 --> 00:02:01,480
It didn't feel great.

47
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:05,440
Ten days later, the charges
against Harold were dropped,

48
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:08,000
and he asked to meet me at the same diner.

49
00:02:08,080 --> 00:02:10,160
He looked smaller in daylight.

50
00:02:10,280 --> 00:02:13,040
"I owe you an explanation," he said.

51
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:13,880
That night,

52
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:17,800
Brandt's security guy had been watching
the pickup spot outside the office,

53
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:20,720
checking every rideshare
car that pulled up.

54
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:24,160
And every one of them had the
app's sticker on the windshield.

55
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:25,680
Except mine.

56
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:30,293
Mine peeled off in a car wash months
ago, and I never bothered to replace it.

57
00:02:30,347 --> 00:02:33,080
"I canceled two cars
because they had stickers,"

58
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:34,320
Harold said.

59
00:02:34,347 --> 00:02:36,800
"Yours looked like somebody's regular car.

60
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:38,520
Nobody would think twice.

61
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:40,520
That's why I asked for your number.

62
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:42,800
And that's why I said I was sorry."

63
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:45,760
Then he slid a business
card across the table.

64
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:47,960
A friend of his ran a delivery company.

65
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:49,400
They needed drivers.

66
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:51,200
Company van included.

67
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:54,040
That's ending two of four.

68
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:56,600
You know why the bag ended up in my car.

69
00:02:56,640 --> 00:02:59,400
But you still don't know
where that money came from.

70
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:01,640
Go back and try another path.

71
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:04,040
The full map is pinned in the comments.
